<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Demo data for an electrical materials distributor in Lima that imports part of its stock:
        the freight and the foreign supplier's invoice arrive after the goods were sold.

        Three situations, the ones this module exists for, each visible afterwards in
        Inventory > Reporting > Late Revaluations with its own journal entry:

          1. Cable NYY 2x4: 5 rolls at 500 billed, 3 sold and invoiced, freight of 250 afterwards.
             -> the delivery is restated to 1,650 and the 150 of the goods already gone are booked
                as cost of sales instead of sitting in the freight account.
          2. LED street lights: received against the proforma and sold, commercial invoice later at
             a lower price. -> the difference goes the other way: without the module the stock
                account ends up below the inventory.
          3. Hex bolts: the counter dispatched 5 hundred with 2 in stock and the receipt of 5 at 20
             was registered afterwards. -> the 30 that Odoo's engine drops on negative stock are
                recorded on that receipt and booked.

        Built through the real flows (see stock.value.revaluation._variance_build_demo), so the
        values, the entries and the events are genuine, not hand-written records.
    -->
    <function model="stock.value.revaluation" name="_variance_build_demo"/>
</odoo>
